<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <title>Namibia 2026 | NODE</title>
  <meta name="description" content="NODE's ASKET vessel in Lüderitz, Namibia, with Kelp Blue: measuring the kelp below the canopy.">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <%- themeCSS %>
</head>
<body>

  <%- include('../partials/nav') %>

  <section class="mission-hero">
    <div class="mission-hero-inner">
      <a class="back-link" href="/missions">&larr; All missions</a>
      <div class="mission-category">Mission · Lüderitz, Namibia</div>
      <h1>Namibia 2026: the kelp below the canopy</h1>
      <p class="mission-lead">The drone sees the canopy. ASKET measures what is below it.</p>
      <dl class="mission-facts">
        <div><dt>Dates</dt><dd>7 November to 2 December 2026</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Host partner</dt><dd>Kelp Blue</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Vessel</dt><dd>ASKET 2.0</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission-section">
    <div class="mission-section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">Purpose</div>
      <p class="mission-text">Kelp Blue cultivates giant kelp forests off the coast of Lüderitz to restore marine ecosystems and produce their biostimulant, StimBlue. To track how the farm grows, they currently estimate biomass using drone imagery. Aerial images only capture the canopy at the surface, though, and much of the kelp’s structure lies underwater, out of the drone’s view.</p>
      <p class="mission-text" style="margin-top:16px">Our mission is to find out whether an autonomous surface vessel can fill that gap. We are deploying ASKET 2.0, our ASV, equipped with Cerulean Sonar’s Omniscan 3D 450 SS and an AI-powered 3D computer vision camera, to survey the kelp beneath the surface. The sonar produces real-time 3D point clouds of the kelp, and the camera footage helps us check and interpret what the sonar detects and guide safe navigation.</p>
      <p class="mission-text" style="margin-top:16px">The goal is a repeatable survey method that adds a subsurface view to Kelp Blue’s drone biomass model, giving a more complete picture of what is growing on the farm.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission-section mission-section-alt">
    <div class="mission-section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">Plan</div>
      <ol class="mission-plan">
        <li><span>Week 1</span><strong>On land</strong><p>Assembly, watertight tests, shore station and sensors.</p></li>
        <li><span>Week 2</span><strong>Harbour</strong><p>Float and leak check, driving, telemetry, sonar and camera calibration.</p></li>
        <li><span>Week 3</span><strong>Navigation and kelp survey</strong><p>Navigation missions on the farm with an escort boat, kelp survey runs and drone flights.</p></li>
        <li><span>Week 4</span><strong>Method and data pipeline</strong><p>Turn the survey runs into a repeatable methodology and a data pipeline from vessel to report.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission-live">
    <div class="mission-live-inner">
      <div class="mission-live-label">Live mission view</div>
      <h2>Follow ASKET on the water</h2>
      <p>When the vessel is out, you can watch its position, route, sonar and camera in a read-only live view.</p>
      <span class="mission-live-btn is-soon" aria-disabled="true">Opens when ASKET is on the water</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission-section">
    <div class="mission-section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">On the ground</div>
      <ul class="mission-team">
        <%
          // Roles as in the Kelp Blue invitation letters. Add each LinkedIn URL;
          // a name without one shows as plain text.
          const crew = [
            { name: 'Francisco Ferrer', role: 'Captain and Mission Lead', linkedin: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/francisco-ferrer-195862152/' },
            { name: 'Belén Comotto', role: 'GUI (Data Mission) and Communications', linkedin: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/belen-comotto-53aaaa197/' },
            { name: 'Lakshmi Narayanan', role: 'Software and GUI (Vehicle Mission)', linkedin: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/lakshmi-narayanan-2b9b75177/' },
            { name: 'Maximilian Becht', role: 'Hardware and Ground Station', linkedin: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/maximilian-becht-61a929207/' },
          ];
        %>
        <% crew.forEach(function(m) { %>
          <li>
            <% if (m.linkedin) { %>
              <a class="crew-link" href="<%= m.linkedin %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong><%= m.name %></strong></a>
            <% } else { %>
              <strong><%= m.name %></strong>
            <% } %>
            <span><%= m.role %></span>
          </li>
        <% }); %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mission-section mission-section-alt">
    <div class="mission-section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">Our partners</div>
      <div class="partners-logos mission-partners">
        <img src="/images/partners/partner-3.svg" alt="Cerulean Sonar" loading="lazy">
        <%# Kelp Blue and Flying Labs logos to come from Belén; names shown until then. %>
        <span class="partner-name">Kelp Blue</span>
        <img src="/images/partners/partner-2.svg" alt="La Máquina" loading="lazy">
        <img src="/images/partners/partner-1.svg" alt="IAAC" loading="lazy">
        <span class="partner-name">Flying Labs Namibia</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('../partials/footer') %>

</body>
</html>
